WEBVTT

00:00.000 --> 00:03.501
Texas law requires all real estate license holders to give the

00:03.501 --> 00:09.562
following information about brokerage services to prospective buyers,
tenants, sellers and landlords.

00:09.762 --> 00:12.282
The Commission writes that notice.

00:12.682 --> 00:13.788
You do not.

00:13.988 --> 00:19.105
This is the current version — Information About Brokerage Services,
form number IABS 1-2.

00:19.305 --> 00:21.421
Let's read it block by block.

00:21.821 --> 00:23.763
Here is the whole notice.

00:23.963 --> 00:30.967
One page, and the revision stamp in the corner reads 11-03-2025 —
that is how you check you are holding the current version.

00:31.167 --> 00:32.902
Notice what it is not.

00:33.102 --> 00:36.742
Not a contract, not a listing, not a representation agreement.

00:36.742 --> 00:39.694
Every block on this page describes a relationship.

00:39.894 --> 00:41.836
None of them creates one.

00:42.036 --> 00:44.137
The first block sets the vocabulary.

00:44.137 --> 00:51.051
A broker is responsible for all brokerage activities, including acts
performed by sales agents sponsored by the broker.

00:51.051 --> 00:56.066
A sales agent must be sponsored by a broker and works with clients on
behalf of the broker.

00:56.066 --> 00:59.388
The broker holds the relationship; you act for the broker.

00:59.388 --> 01:03.994
Now the duties block — and read the heading
including the words in parentheses.

01:03.994 --> 01:07.414
A client is the person or party that the broker represents.

01:07.414 --> 01:12.090
That parenthesis does real work, because the Act
itself never defines the word.

01:12.090 --> 01:15.301
Three of the four bullets beneath it run to that client.

01:15.301 --> 01:19.000
Put the interests of the client above all others, including the

01:19.000 --> 01:23.188
broker's own interests; Inform the client of any material information

01:23.188 --> 01:27.236
about the property or transaction received by the broker; Answer the

01:27.236 --> 01:31.843
client's questions and present any offer to or
counter-offer from the client.

01:32.043 --> 01:34.017
The fourth bullet does not.

01:34.217 --> 01:37.872
Treat all parties to a real estate transaction honestly and fairly.

01:38.072 --> 01:40.046
Three duties to the client.

01:40.246 --> 01:42.490
One owed to everybody in the transaction.

01:42.690 --> 01:45.113
Representation decides advocacy.

01:45.513 --> 01:47.616
It has never decided honesty.

01:47.816 --> 01:53.229
The next block is headed, a license holder can represent a party in a
real estate transaction.

01:53.229 --> 01:57.046
As agent for owner: the broker becomes the property owner's agent

01:57.046 --> 02:03.361
through an agreement with the owner, usually in a written listing to
sell or property management agreement.

02:03.361 --> 02:06.787
As agent for buyer or tenant: the broker becomes the buyer or

02:06.787 --> 02:12.885
tenant's agent by agreeing to represent the buyer, usually through a
written representation agreement.

02:12.885 --> 02:17.681
Both paragraphs close the same way — fees are not
set by law and are fully negotiable.

02:17.881 --> 02:19.797
Two more blocks finish the page.

02:20.197 --> 02:22.166
As agent for both — intermediary.

02:22.366 --> 02:28.337
And below it, when a license holder can show property without
representing the buyer or tenant.

02:28.537 --> 02:30.977
Later modules take both apart.

02:31.177 --> 02:33.566
Today, know where they sit on the page.

02:33.566 --> 02:35.872
At the foot is the block students skip.

02:35.872 --> 02:39.330
This notice is being provided for information purposes.

02:39.330 --> 02:43.510
It does not create an obligation for you to use the broker's services.

02:43.510 --> 02:49.563
Then four contact rows, each with a licence number — which is why a
completed notice carries several.

02:49.563 --> 02:52.517
And a line for the consumer's initials and a date.

02:52.717 --> 02:55.163
Initials acknowledge receipt.

02:55.563 --> 02:58.081
They are not consent to anything.

02:58.481 --> 03:00.136
One page, three jobs.

03:00.336 --> 03:07.589
It names the license types, states the broker's minimum duties, and
describes every relationship a Texas broker may lawfully occupy.

03:07.789 --> 03:10.022
What it never does is create one.

03:10.222 --> 03:12.405
A relationship comes from an agreement.

03:12.605 --> 03:14.517
This comes from a statute.
